Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): share archive preflight deadline across
 sequential reads [daveey]

Five-whys continuation for PR4013 review6011021833:
1. Reconnect exhaustion could show Archive anyway because the preflight watchdog
   returned unknown while a transport read was still pending.
2. A successful ancestry read spent 1000ms, but the next task read still received
   the original 5000ms remaining budget; 250ms grace only protected the first read.
3. Each request derived its timeout from the attempt's input rather than an
   absolute deadline shared by ancestry, tasks and the one legacy timeout retry.
4. Tests exercised a single timed-out read, not sequential success then timeout
   on the ninth/final reconnect attempt. The hung-read test even expected override.
5. Safety uncertainty and transport exhaustion shared the watchdog's resolved
   unknown path, allowing a safety dialog to conceal exhausted connectivity.

Calculate remaining time before every send/retry and reject late successful
results too. Retry-mode watchdog exhaustion is a reconnect error, not permission
to override; legacy nontransport unknown confirmation remains unchanged. Late
ancestry cannot issue another request after settlement/deadline.

Proof: three regression tests fail on1c5a1b30 (including real archivePreflight
restoration/no-dialog); late successful task result fails on intermediate fix.
Final GREEN530 tests/43 action modules; TypeScript and ESLint pass; scripts/check
all21 pass. Fresh exact-head CI/review required. Passive laptop-1 acceptance
remains unproven; no launch or fault injection.
